TUnit uses `[Before(…)]` / `[After(…)]` attributes with a **hook type** to control scope, plus `[ClassDataSource]` for fixtures. Here's each level:

---

### 1. Before / after every test in the class

```csharp
public class OrderTests
{
    [Before(Test)]
    public void ResetDatabase()
    {
        InMemoryDb.Reset();
    }

    [After(Test)]
    public void Cleanup()
    {
        InMemoryDb.Clear();
    }

    [Test]
    public async Task Order_IsCreated() { /* … */ }
}
```

---

### 2. Once before first / after last test in a class

```csharp
public class OrderTests
{
    [Before(Class)]
    public static void OpenFixture()
    {
        // Runs once before the first test in this class
    }

    [After(Class)]
    public static void DisposeFixture()
    {
        // Runs once after the last test in this class
    }

    [Test]
    public async Task Order_IsCreated() { /* … */ }
}
```

`[Before(Class)]` / `[After(Class)]` methods **must be `static`**.

---

### 3. Once per assembly

```csharp
public class GlobalSetup
{
    [Before(Assembly)]
    public static void StartWireMock()
    {
        // Runs once before any test in this assembly
    }

    [After(Assembly)]
    public static void StopWireMock()
    {
        // Runs once after all tests in this assembly
    }
}
```

The class can live anywhere in the assembly — TUnit discovers it by the attribute.

---

### 4. Once per entire test session (cross-assembly)

```csharp
public class SessionSetup
{
    [Before(TestSession)]
    public static void ApplyMigrations()
    {
        // Very first thing to run
    }

    [After(TestSession)]
    public static void TearDownDatabase()
    {
        // Very last thing to run
    }
}
```

---

### Summary table

| Scope | Attribute | Must be static? |
|---|---|---|
| Each test | `[Before(Test)]` / `[After(Test)]` | No |
| Class (once) | `[Before(Class)]` / `[After(Class)]` | Yes |
| Assembly (once) | `[Before(Assembly)]` / `[After(Assembly)]` | Yes |
| Session (once) | `[Before(TestSession)]` / `[After(TestSession)]` | Yes |

The enum values (`Test`, `Class`, `Assembly`, `TestSession`) come from `TUnit.Core.HookType`. All hooks support `async Task` return types as well.
